---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";

const title = "Refund & Cancellation Policy | Dicot Innovations";
const description =
  "Refund and cancellation rules for Dicot software licences, cloud subscriptions and duplicate transactions, including processing timelines.";
---
<Legal
  title={title}
  description={description}
  label="Refund & cancellation"
  lede="Software licences and cloud subscriptions are digital products. This page explains when an order can be cancelled or refunded."
>
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 18 November 2026 · <strong>Version:</strong> 2.0</p>

  <h2>1. Cancellation before delivery</h2>
  <p>
    If you cancel an order before a licence key is generated or a cloud subscription is activated, the order amount is
    refunded in full. Cancel by writing to <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.sales}`}>{site.emails.sales}</a> with the order
    or invoice number.
  </p>

  <h2>2. After a licence is generated</h2>
  <p>
    A software licence cannot be cancelled or refunded once the licence key has been issued, because the product can be
    used immediately. This applies to Vision C, Vision S, VGraphic and cloud activations.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Cloud subscriptions</h2>
  <p>
    Cloud subscriptions are paid in advance. Cancellation stops the next renewal; the current period is not refunded.
    If you cancel, export your data before the period ends. We retain cloud data as described in the
    <a href="/legal/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and your order terms.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Physical goods</h2>
  <p>
    If a physical item has shipped but has not been delivered, the order can be cancelled and the amount refunded after
    deducting shipping and handling, once the item is returned intact. Delivered items cannot be cancelled.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Failed or duplicate transactions</h2>
  <p>
    If a payment fails but money is debited, or the same order is charged twice, the affected amount is refunded. Send
    the transaction reference and invoice number to <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.sales}`}>{site.emails.sales}</a>.
    Bank or card charges may not be refundable.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Processing time</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds are processed within 5–7 business days on our side. Your bank or card issuer may take longer to
    credit the amount. We cannot guarantee a specific credit date once the refund leaves us.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Partial cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    Where an order includes multiple items and only some are cancelled, the refund corresponds to the cancelled part.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The version on this page applies to orders placed after its effective date.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name}<br />
    {site.address.full}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.sales}`}>{site.emails.sales}</a> · {site.phones[0].label}
  </p>
</Legal>
